question:
Solve the following system of equations for $c$:
\begin{align*}
a - b &= 2 (c+d)\\
b &= a-2 \\
d &= c+5
\end{align*}

Let $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ $d,$ and $e$ be the distinct roots of the equation $x^5 + 7x^4 - 2 = 0.$  Find
\begin{align*}
&\frac{a^3}{(a - b)(a - c)(a - d)(a - e)} + \frac{b^3}{(b - a)(b - c)(b - d)(b - e)} \\
&\quad + \frac{c^3}{(c - a)(c - b)(c - d)(c - e)} + \frac{d^3}{(d - a)(d - b)(d - c)(d - e)} \\
&\quad + \frac{e^3}{(e - a)(e - b)(e - c)(e - d)}.
\end{align*}

For integers $n$, let \[f(n) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
n^2 & \text{ if }n\text{ is odd}, \\
n^2 - 4n - 1 & \text{ if }n\text{ is even}.
\end{array}
\right.\]Find $f(f(f(f(f(4)))))$.
